{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1980,2110p' src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc; rg -n \\\"linked|requires|require.*py|yang.call\\\" src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/publication.cljc test/cljc/yang/python/antlr; rg -n \\\"closure.*total|per-lane|shared count|union|gate_test|jolt\\\" test src/dev .\"","aggregated_output":";; assignment and an annotation carry more.\n(defn- display-statement\n  \"The id of the last top-level bare expression statement of the module,\n   the one a REPL submission displays (Clojure's last expression evaluated;\n   an assignment is a statement and displays nothing), or nil.\"\n  [pk]\n  (let [expr-stmts (for [stmt (p/child-rules pk (p/root pk) \"stmt\")\n                         simple (p/child-rules pk\n                                               (first (p/children pk stmt))\n                                               \"simple_stmt\")\n                         :let [e (first (p/children pk simple))]\n                         :when (and (p/rule? e \"expr_stmt\")\n                                    (= 1 (count (p/children pk e))))]\n                     (:id e))]\n    (last expr-stmts)))\n\n\n(defn- context\n  [packet unit display?]\n  (let [pk (p/validate! packet {:diagnostic-ns diagnostic-ns})\n        analysis (scope/analyze pk)]\n    {:pk pk,\n     :display-id (when display? (display-statement pk)),\n     :unit unit,\n     :importlib-bindings (importlib-bindings pk),\n     :lines (newline-lines pk),\n     :max-digits (digit-budget packet),\n     :analysis analysis,\n     :scope (:module analysis),\n     :lower lower,\n     :loop nil,\n     :ret nil,\n     :exc nil,\n     :class nil,\n     :gen nil,\n     :comp nil}))\n\n\n(defn lower-module-body\n  \"The module's statements as one node, before the runtime wrapper: what\n   lowering goldens compare. `unit`, the unit's declared `{:name\n   :package?}`, resolves its relative imports; nil (the default, as for\n   `__main__`) is a packageless unit.\"\n  ([packet] (lower-module-body packet nil))\n  ([packet unit] (lower-module-body packet unit false))\n  ([packet unit display?]\n   (let [ctx (context packet unit display?)]\n     (lower ctx (p/root (:pk ctx))))))\n\n\n(defn lower-packet\n  \"The complete program for one ok packet: the module body run by\n   `py/run-main`, with tail calls marked. Its value is `{:py/out [...]\n   :py/exception nil-or-{:type :args}}`. The packet may declare the\n   decimal digit budget of its literals as `:yang.python.antlr/max-digits`.\n\n   `:prelude` selects how the runtime profile arrives: `:bundled` (the\n   default) carries the prelude tree ahead of the body; `:linked`\n   requires `yang.call` and `py` from the task's link pair, then allocates\n   the task's runtime state with `(py/init!)`. Either way the body names only\n   `py/` exports, never a runtime key.\n\n   Guest imports deliver through try-require thunks at the executed\n   statement, after checking sys.modules. Only py is eagerly required;\n   an import-free unit's tree is unchanged. The program is __main__, a\n   packageless unit, so its relative imports raise. Imports need the linked\n   prelude -- a module closure's free reads never see the ambient store,\n   so a bundled importer's `py/*` definitions are invisible to an\n   imported body -- and a bundled unit holding any import statement but\n   a plain import of sys, builtins or importlib is refused. Literal\n   import_module calls that deliver guest modules need the linked profile.\"\n  ([packet] (lower-packet packet {}))\n  ([packet {:keys [prelude], :or {prelude :bundled}}]\n   (let [pk (p/validate! packet {:diagnostic-ns diagnostic-ns})\n         main (app* 'py/run-main\n                    (u/lam [globals-sym globals-fn-sym]\n                           (lower-module-body packet)))]\n     (u/mark-tails\n       (case prelude\n         :bundled (if-not (preseeded-imports-only? pk)\n                    (throw (ex-info\n                             \"Imports need the linked prelude (docs/design/yang.antlr.md 8.5.6)\"\n                             {:yang.python.antlr/diagnostic :yang.python.antlr/unsupported,\n                              :construct \"import under the bundled prelude\"}))\n                    (u/then prelude/uast main))\n         :linked (u/seq-nodes\n                   [(app* 'require (u/lit 'yang.call))\n                    (app* 'require (u/lit prelude/module-name))\n                    (app* 'py/init!) main]))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The module emitter: one Python unit as the linker module pym.<name>\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private require-node core-module/require-node)\n\n\n(def module-exports\n  \"The exports of a compiled Python unit: its spec and body, immutable\n   after install (docs/design/yang.antlr.md 8.5.6's module shape).\"\n  '#{spec body})\n\n\n(defn- validate-module-name!\n  [name]\n  (when (or (empty? name)\n            (str/starts-with? name \".\")\n            (str/ends-with? name \".\")\n            (str/includes? name \"..\")\n            (str/includes? name \"$\"))\n    (throw (ex-info \"a module name is dotted identifiers\"\n                    {:yang.python.antlr/diagnostic :yang.python.antlr/unsupported,\n                     :construct \"malformed module name\",\n                     :name name}))))\n\n\n(defn module-packet\n  \"One ok packet as the linker module `pym.<mangled>`: one wide\n   application whose operands are `(require 'py)`, then the spec and\n   body definitions. Guest imports deliver at statement time; module-spec\n   still pins every static import. `name` is\n   the dotted Python module name and `package?` (default false) whether\n   the unit is a package, which is source layout, not derivable from\n   rows: the spec records both, the runtime derives `__package__` from\n   them, and the lowering resolves relative imports against them. The\n   body is the same form `lower-packet` runs as `__main__`: one code\n   image, two roles.\"\n  [packet {:keys [name package?]}]\n  (validate-module-name! name)\n  (let [unit {:name name, :package? (boolean package?)}\nrg: test/cljc/yang/python/antlr: No such file or directory (os error 2)\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:37:     `(require 'pym.m)` hoisted per import in the program wrapper (linked\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2037:   default) carries the prelude tree ahead of the body; `:linked`\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2038:   requires `yang.call` and `py` from the task's link pair, then allocates\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2045:   packageless unit, so its relative imports raise. Imports need the linked\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2050:   import_module calls that deliver guest modules need the linked profile.\"\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2061:                             \"Imports need the linked prelude (docs/design/yang.antlr.md 8.5.6)\"\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2065:         :linked (u/seq-nodes\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2066:                   [(app* 'require (u/lit 'yang.call))\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2099:   application whose operands are `(require 'py)`, then the spec and\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2143:   covered by that requirement, discharged by a linked module of equal\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2199:   Alias :requires is filled with the bundle address after publication.\"\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2266:        ;; sibling bindings before require; defining the lambdas runs no py.\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2318:   default, or `:linked`) is `lower-packet`'s. Stateless.\"\nsrc/dev/jolt_json_shim_check.cljc:1:;; Tests of the jolt clojure.data.json shim (src/jolt/clojure/data/json.jolt).\nsrc/dev/jolt_json_shim_che