 gate r2 found the last edge: the ruling covered holders but not CANDIDATES with an unavailable inbox. glm's usage cap killed the sol fix; opus (the gate itself) fixed it from the worktree cwd, and fable CONFIRMED the candidate semantics (collab/1791389000000-architect-d15a-candidate-confirm-fable.stdout.log: an :activating candidate still stops at its own lease bound — verified in the code path). (7) Three-lane exit 0 on the final tree (JVM 3668/238519, Node 3523/103021, Dart green). An earlier concurrent-run Node failure (2 store_test assertions) did not reproduce on the settled tree — contention-induced.\n./docs/orchestrator-log.md:10935:        * `c3_gate_test.cljc`: added `linked-equals-bundled-test` across all 4 VMs.\n./docs/orchestrator-log.md:11086:  (1) `docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md`: the transported state of UCF as positional rows with merkle ids (body version 3, semantic profile only). Owner rulings encoded: semantic-VM safepoints; state as tuples; tuples transport-only, execution native. Design choices (labelled as proposals in §10): body version 3 with the existing outer gate; two id spaces (content rows / identity cells) with a root-committed cell census; disjoint [:lit|:row|:cell] value union; closed row table mirroring the v2 body (ordered waits, parked table, installs with child tasks, custody arm by role/kind/policy, r5 pending union with op-ids, env bindings + store-of); canonical cell numbering defined as the output of a renaming-invariant refinement-and-search byte procedure with validation by re-emission; validation in amendment §8 order; three parity laws with explicit domains; SHA-256 pinned for row ids.\n./docs/orchestrator-log.md:12080:  commissioned; the wasm32 profile section for yin.vm.rust and a post-K0 jolt (Chez) spike are\n./docs/orchestrator-log.md:12087:  feasibility), the wasm32 profile section, the jolt spike decision.\n./docs/orchestrator-log.md:12216:## 2026-10-19 22:15:00 +0700 — jolt host-lane seat: spike verifi