{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,48p' src/dev/host_boundary/closure.clj; sed -n '270,320p' src/dev/host_boundary/closure.clj; sed -n '1,45p' docs/design/host-boundary/closure-clj.edn; sed -n '1,100p' src/cljc/yang/core/module.cljc 2>/dev/null || rg -n \\\"defn module-spec|defn module-tree|require-node\\\" src/cljc/yang/core\"","aggregated_output":"(ns host-boundary.closure\n  \"The adopted closure of dao.stream.host-boundary.md §3.1, per lane.\n\n   A require-form traversal from yin.repl.main over the ns declarations,\n   parsed by clojure.tools.namespace.parse (read-ns-decl with the lane's\n   reader features, deps-from-ns-decl for :require, :use and\n   :require-macros; :as-alias and string (npm, dart:) libspecs are not\n   dependencies). Lane features: :clj #{:clj}, :cljs #{:cljs},\n   :cljd #{:cljd :clj} (the cljd build also reads :clj arms; the first\n   matching arm wins, as in tools.reader). A namespace resolves to\n   src/<lane>/<path>.<lane> first (the shadow: yin.repl.host is\n   host.cljc on the JVM, host.cljs and host.cljd elsewhere), then\n   src/cljc/<path>.cljc; a namespace with neither (clojure.core, a\n   library) is outside the closure.\n\n   It is not a compiler-resolved call graph: it over-includes a namespace\n   required but unused, and does not see dynamic loading.\n\n   Each file is tagged with its §3.1 classes (a set: a file can sit in\n   several rows of the §3.1 table; :none means no host contact beyond the\n   §3.3 exempt syntax).\n\n   Run from the repo root:\n     clojure -Sdeps '{:aliases {:hb {:extra-paths [\\\"src/dev\\\"]\n                      :extra-deps {org.clojure/tools.namespace\n                                   {:mvn/version \\\"1.5.0\\\"}}}}}' \\\\\n       -M:hb -m host-boundary.closure [--check]\n   writes docs/design/host-boundary/closure-{clj,cljs,cljd}.edn and\n   prints the totals; --check writes nothing and exits 1 when a committed\n   file differs from the computed closure.\n\n   `--required-by NS` (slice H2's pre- and post-deletion gate) writes\n   nothing: it reads the ns form of every source file under src/ and\n   test/ on each lane that reads the file, prints each file whose ns\n   form requires NS, and exits 0 when none does, 1 when some file does,\n   and 2 when it read no file or could not read one (a scan failure is\n   never \\\"none found\\\").\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.java.io :as io]\n    [clojure.pprint :as pp]\n    [clojure.set :as set]\n    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [clojure.tools.namespace.parse :as parse]\n    [clojure.walk :as walk]))\n\n\n(def root 'yin.repl.main)\n(def lanes [:clj :cljs :cljd])\n(defn- required-by-main\n  [ns-name]\n  (let [{:keys [files requirers errors]} (required-by (symbol ns-name))]\n    (println (format \"required-by %s: read %d files under %s\" ns-name (count files)\n                     (str/join \" \" source-roots)))\n    (doseq [[f err] errors] (println \"SCAN ERROR:\" f err))\n    (doseq [f requirers] (println \"REQUIRES:\" f))\n    (cond\n      (or (empty? files) (seq errors)) (do (println \"SCAN FAILURE\") (System/exit 2))\n      (seq requirers) (System/exit 1)\n      :else (do (println \"none\") (shutdown-agents)))))\n\n\n(defn- closure-main\n  [args]\n  (let [check? (some #{\"--check\"} args)\n        {:keys [shared reports]} (compute)\n        stale (atom [])]\n    (doseq [l lanes]\n      (let [r (reports l)\n            text (render r)\n            f (io/file (out-file l))]\n        (println (format \"%-5s total %d shared %d lane-specific %d\"\n                         (name l) (:total r) (:shared r) (:lane-specific r)))\n        (if check?\n          (when-not (and (.isFile f) (= text (slurp f)))\n            (swap! stale conj (out-file l)))\n          (do (io/make-parents f)\n              (spit f text)))))\n    (println \"shared (all three lanes):\" (count shared))\n    (when (seq @stale)\n      (println \"STALE:\" (str/join \" \" @stale))\n      (System/exit 1))\n    (shutdown-agents)))\n\n\n(defn -main\n  [& args]\n  (if-let [ns-name (second (drop-while #(not= \"--required-by\" %) args))]\n    (required-by-main ns-name)\n    (closure-main args)))\n;; Generated by src/dev/host_boundary/closure.clj (host-boundary H0).\n;; Do not edit by hand; regenerate with the command in that file's ns doc.\n{:lane :clj,\n :root yin.repl.main,\n :features #{:clj},\n :total 156,\n :shared 148,\n :lane-specific 8,\n :class-legend\n {:codec-track \"codec track, untouched (§8.3)\",\n  :consumer \"H2 (require change only)\",\n  :deferred-entropy \"deferred §9.1\",\n  :deferred-gensym \"deferred §9.1\",\n  :deferred-stage \"deferred §9.3\",\n  :deferred-storage \"deferred §9.2\",\n  :deferred-timers \"deferred §9.1\",\n  :dialect-arm \"none (H0 finding: retained dialect arms)\",\n  :driver \"driver (ambient reads deferred §9.1)\",\n  :external-stream-seam \"none (existing streams)\",\n  :internal-pure-display \"none (list 1, display only)\",\n  :none \"no host contact beyond §3.3\",\n  :profile-consumer \"H2 (H0 finding: consumers of table A entries)\",\n  :profile-hash-sign \"H3\",\n  :profile-internal-pure\n  \"H1-H2 (writer H4); the dao.host profile (H1, reached at H2)\",\n  :runtime-prereq \"table C, no slice\"},\n :files\n [{:file \"src/clj/dao/jing/content/driver.clj\",\n   :ns dao.jing.content.driver,\n   :shared false,\n   :classes #{:deferred-timers}}\n  {:file \"src/clj/dao/stream/datagram/jvm.clj\",\n   :ns dao.stream.datagram.jvm,\n   :shared false,\n   :classes #{:external-stream-seam}}\n  {:file \"src/clj/dao/stream/waitset/driver.clj\",\n   :ns dao.stream.waitset.driver,\n   :shared false,\n   :classes #{:external-stream-seam}}\n  {:file \"src/clj/dao/stream/ws/jvm.clj\",\n   :ns dao.stream.ws.jvm,\n   :shared false,\n   :classes #{:codec-track :external-stream-seam}}\n  {:file \"src/clj/yang/antlr/cst.clj\",\n   :ns yang.antlr.cst,\n(ns yang.core.module\n  \"Module emitter machinery shared by every language frontend\n   (docs/design/yang.typescript.md §17, lift L3): the linker module naming\n   rule, the `require` and wide-application tree nodes, free-name\n   declaration over a host registry, and the `module-spec` and SCC bundle\n   shapes `yin.vm.linker.publish/publish-module!` takes. A language supplies\n   its prefix, its runtime module and its module AST; nothing here knows a\n   source language.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [yang.core.prelude :as prelude]\n    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]\n    [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n\n\n(defn module-symbol\n  \"The linker module name of source module `name` under language `prefix`\n   (\\\"py\\\", \\\"php\\\", \\\"js\\\"): `<prefix>m.` then the name with each dot a `$`,\n   so no linker module name is a dotted prefix of another.\"\n  [prefix name]\n  (symbol (str prefix \"m.\" (str/replace name \".\" \"$\"))))\n\n\n(defn require-node\n  \"(require 'm) as a tree node.\"\n  [m]\n  (u/sexp->uast (list 'require (list 'quote m))))\n\n\n(defn module-tree\n  \"A wide application: all definitions remain at module level.\"\n  [operands]\n  (prelude/wide-app operands))\n\n\n(defn declare-free-name\n  \"The `:primitives` entry free name `n` declares over `registry`, or nil\n   when `covered` (the requirement-pinned module names) covers it. A name\n   no `vm/primitives` profile or host export supplies throws, with\n   `refusal` under `refusal-key` in its data.\"\n  [refusal-key refusal registry covered n]\n  (if (and (symbol? n) (some? (namespace n))\n           (contains? covered (symbol (namespace n))))\n    nil\n    (if-let [profile (vm/profile-of vm/primitives n)]\n      [n profile]\n      (if-let [address (module/host-export-profile registry n)]\n        (let [entry (module/module-entry (:modules registry)\n                                         (symbol (namespace n)))\n              f (get-in entry [:slice (symbol (name n))])]\n          [n {:yin.k/profile address,\n              :yin.k/effects\n              (get (:callable-effects registry) f #{})}])\n        (throw (ex-info \"the module reads an undeclared name\"\n                        {refusal-key refusal, :name n}))))))\n\n\n(defn free-primitives\n  \"The `:primitives` map declaring every free name of `ast` over `registry`.\"\n  [refusal-key refusal registry covered ast]\n  (let [free (remove (conj (prelude/defined-keys ast) 'yin/def)\n                     (prelude/free-names ast))]\n    (into {}\n          (keep (partial declare-free-name refusal-key refusal registry covered))\n          (sort-by str free))))\n\n\n(defn module-spec\n  \"`publish-module!`'s spec for module `name`: `ast` with `exports`, requiring\n   the runtime module `runtime-name` at `runtime-address` and each of `deps`\n   ({module-symbol address}). A free name under a required module is covered\n   by it; any other is declared as `declare-free-name` does.\"\n  [refusal-key refusal registry\n   {:keys [name ast exports runtime-name runtime-address deps]}]\n  (let [requires (into {runtime-name runtime-address} deps)]\n    {:name name,\n     :ast ast,\n     :exports exports,\n     :requires requires,\n     :primitives (free-primitives refusal-key refusal registry\n                                  (set (keys requires)) ast)}))\n\n\n(defn alias-spec\n  \"A thin member alias of the SCC bundle `bundle-name`: it requires the\n   bundle and defines `spec` and `body` as the bundle's `spec-key` and\n   `body-key` exports.\"\n  [name exports require-profile bundle-name spec-key body-key]\n  {:name name,\n   :exports exports,\n   :primitives {'require require-profile},\n   :ast (module-tree\n          [(require-node bundle-name)\n           (u/def! 'spec (u/v (symbol (str bundle-name) (str spec-key))))\n           (u/def! 'body (u/v (symbol (str bundle-name) (str body-key))))])})\n\n\n(defn scc-module-specs\n  \"The SCC publication shape: the `bundle` spec first, then the member alias\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
