{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_106","type":"agent_message","text":"The publication regression run found a harness issue: an unconditional test-harness `yang.call` preload breaks tests that intentionally use a minimal `py` module and an empty content store. I removed that global preload, kept the production lowerer’s explicit call-before-py emission, and made the one hand-written runtime fixture request `yang.call` before `py`. I’m rerunning publication tests after that correction."}}
