{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_149","type":"agent_message","text":"**Linked-path fix:** ordinary module emission skipped `yang.call`. `py`’s manifest pinned it, but `py`’s module AST never required it, so the dependency wasn’t available inside `py`’s closure. I added `require yang.call` to the `py` module tree and made ordinary and SCC source modules require and pin it before `py` when their bodies reference the convention.\n\n**Post-J6e totals:** the mechanical closure check matches the existing constants and ledgers:\n\n- JVM: **156 total**, 148 shared, 8 lane-specific\n- ClojureScript: **154 total**, 148 shared, 6 lane-specific\n- ClojureDart: **155 total**, 148 shared, 7 lane-specific\n- Shared: **148**; union: **168**\n\nNo totals files needed changes.\n\n**Generator:** ran with `deferred #{:py :pysp}` twice; both runs produced identical bytes (SHA-256 `566daad81066a3f3a7d8b5c8df4dc9552d66af191fbf1471ac7bacf9fd1560fa`). The expected `:py` scanner pin changed; `:pysp` did not. Restored the generator declaration to `#{:pysp}`.\n\n**Verification:** import test passed unfiltered, including slow bodies (**50 tests, 436 assertions**). Float address (**12/105**), call-entry (**3/12**), call (**4/15**), and publication (**10/85**) passed. Kondo reported 0 errors and 0 warnings; cljstyle and closure-ledger checks passed.\n\n**Open:** `yin.repl.main-test` could not run because the sandbox denied its socket bind (`Operation not permitted`). I could not commit: the managed filesystem denies writes to the worktree’s Git index outside the writable checkout. The changes remain uncommitted on `python-s3-wiring`; I did not push or touch `master`. Two pre-existing untracked collaboration files remain untouched."}}
